[["The living, 2026-10-14, on what a book carries (STT)" "The book is really about the proposal. I don't need to get all of the verbatim quotes that are used to create the crystallization. I don't want to read all that. I don't even want to [go] through it. I don't see the point.\n\nLike I've said what I've said. Now the machine's job is to crystallize what I've said and that's what I'm interested in doing."] ["The living, 2026-10-14, book comment on «Communicating with the living» (STT)" "We don't need to say \"carries his words.\" That's also a repetition. We don't need to say \"it names the records it draws from.\" I don't want to see the records it draws from.\n\nAlthough if the proposal is accepted there has to be a place. Each book needs to have an associated reference, which is not rendered but which is kept with the source of the book, which would be in text, like the unrendered book. We need the references to be archived accordingly if some or all of the proposal is accepted."] ["The living, 2026-10-14, to d68c82, with a screenshot of the Clojure-migration book showing «His words, 2026-09-25, flows/88475f/...» and «The machine's count, flows/d68c82/reports/...» (STT)" "So do you think that I wasn't clear enough on the fact that I didn't want stuff like this in the book?"]]
